menu "My UPS Pal fleet heartbeat"

config UPSA_FLEET_URL
    string "Fleet heartbeat endpoint (Supabase project URL)"
    default ""
    help
        The Supabase project URL, e.g. https://abcd.supabase.co. The board
        calls its heartbeat() function there. Empty: the heartbeat is built
        in but never sends, and the page says it is not configured.

config UPSA_FLEET_KEY
    string "Fleet heartbeat public key"
    default ""
    help
        The project's PUBLIC (anon / publishable) key. It ships in open-source
        firmware, so it must only be able to call heartbeat(): see
        telemetry/supabase.sql. Never the service_role key.

config UPSA_FLEET_DISABLED
    bool "Never start the check-in at all"
    default n
    help
        Stronger than leaving the endpoint empty. With no URL the task still
        runs and finds nothing to do, costing a 6 KB stack for a feature that
        will never be used; with this set, fleet_start() returns before
        creating it.

        For a deployment that has decided it does not want fleet reporting at
        all, rather than one that has not configured it yet. The page reports
        it as not configured either way, and nothing can turn it on without a
        rebuild.

endmenu
